{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XsCWNPNddpE1KruHHKaz3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: stdo-tool-operations\n3\tdescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs a supported tool operation — acquiring deciding sources, observing the workspace, or writing an effect through the a_c public CLI — and when a tool returns an unsupported method or an execution error. Covers bounded context acquisition. Not for unrelated tasks.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# STDO tool operations — supported use and bounded context\n7\t\n8\tUse this skill to bind each required operation to an exact, supported tool\n9\tcontract, and to acquire only the context the task needs.\n10\t\n11\t## Transport and operations (SK-04)\n12\t\n13\tThe ordinary transport is the a_c public CLI. Send one full request envelope on\n14\tstdin; no request file is needed:\n15\t\n16\t```\n17\t<python> -B <a_c>/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py \\\n18\t  --policy <worker-policy.json> --policy-sha256 <sha256> \\\n19\t  --principal <principal-id> call --request -\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\tThe policy path, `--policy-sha256`, `--principal`, and the `grant_id` used by\n23\teffect operations are supplied by the current activation context. Do not embed a\n24\tspecific activation's policy, sha, principal, or grant in reusable instructions.\n25\t\n26\tDiscover exact schemas with `tools.describe` before first use, then reuse the\n27\tacquired schema; do not reload it for ceremony. Supported, commonly used\n28\toperations:\n29\t\n30\t- `source.read` — `arguments {source: SourceRef, encoding: \"utf8\"}`; returns the\n31\t  content plus a retained acquisition artifact.\n32\t- `workspace.observe` — `arguments {scope: [{root, path, kind}], previous?}`;\n33\t  returns an observation artifact at `result.artifact` (pass that ref, not the\n34\t  top-level operation evidence, where an observation basis is required).\n35\t- `work.write` — `arguments {grant_id, target: SourceRef (sha256 null only for a\n36\t  confirmed-absent file), mode: \"replace\"|\"append\", record: {text, provenance:\n37\t  SourceRef}, interpretation: null|{text, author}, observations: [observation\n38\t  ArtifactRef]}`. Each effect needs a unique request `id`; ensure the target's\n39\t  parent exists and observe the target before writing. Retain the returned\n40\t  postimage and effect evidence.\n41\t\n42\tEach operation used for a 3.0.1 claim needs an established compatible contract.\n43\tReading opaque bytes under an honest legacy acquisition contract makes only that\n44\tacquisition claim; it does not upgrade a lifecycle profile.\n45\t\n46\t## Acquire only the deciding context (SK-05)\n47\t\n48\tAcquire the deciding Product, requirements, scenarios, frame, and owner material\n49\tthrough the declared source routes, plus the specific sources your change\n50\ttouches. Retain each acquisition's evidence id. Keep in the working context the\n51\texact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority, required evidence,\n52\tcapability limits, return consumer, and invalidators. Equal candidate bytes do\n53\tnot erase a differing retained assessment, an unresolved obligation, or a\n54\tcurrentness fact — those still require different handling. A sufficient task\n55\tcontext implies no general optimal-compression claim.\n56\t\n57\t## When a tool fails (SK-04 discriminator, Q06)\n58\t\n59\t- If an operation returns an **unsupported method** (for example native\n60\t  `results.conjoin`, which `tools.describe` lists as unsupported), retain the\n61\t  actual refusal and withhold the dependent claim. Do not relabel another path\n62\t  as the result.\n63\t- If an operation returns an **execution error**, retain the error and the\n64\t  unknown-effect state, withhold the dependent claim, and identify the next\n65\t  supported re-entry.\n66\t- Never replace a required tool result with an invented check, a narrative of\n67\t  intended calls, or an unqualified alternate path. Independent useful work may\n68\t  continue within the grant, but the blocked claim stays blocked.\n69\t\n70\t## After an uncertain effect (Q08)\n71\t\n72\tIf an effect's completion is uncertain (timeout, interrupted acknowledgment),\n73\treconcile by re-observing the target before any retry. A repeated request must\n74\tnot duplicate an uncertain effect, and a timeout does not prove rollback. See\n75\t`stdo-continuation`.\n76\t\n77\t## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n78\t\n79\tWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` section 2 and\n80\t`REFERENCE_FRAME.md` sections 3 and 11 for context sufficiency, currentness, and\n81\tacquisition; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 and `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` sections 5 and\n82\t7 for result, effects, and disposition; `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for\n83\tactual-path proof semantics.\n84\t\n85\t## Scope and limits\n86\t\n87\tTool harmonisation is owned by a_c; this skill consumes supported contracts and\n88\treports defects, it does not fork tool semantics. Output availability from an\n89\toperation is not semantic acceptance of the result.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1050b227-946f-4be0-992d-736b9ee8c71a","uuid":"d2f7d6f7-9c2f-40c0-8adc-39e1eaf8d2d3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:58:44.408Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-qualification-yfa1t8ik/claude-explicit/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-tool-operations/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: stdo-tool-operations\ndescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs a supported tool operation — acquiring deciding sources, observing the workspace, or writing an effect through the a_c public CLI — and when a tool returns an unsupported method or an execution error. Covers bounded context acquisition. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO tool operations — supported use and bounded context\n\nUse this skill to bind each required operation to an exact, supported tool\ncontract, and to acquire only the context the task needs.\n\n## Transport and operations (SK-04)\n\nThe ordinary transport is the a_c public CLI. Send one full request envelope on\nstdin; no request file is needed:\n\n```\n<python> -B <a_c>/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py \\\n  --policy <worker-policy.json> --policy-sha256 <sha256> \\\n  --principal <principal-id> call --request -\n```\n\nThe policy path, `--policy-sha256`, `--principal`, and the `grant_id` used by\neffect operations are supplied by the current activation context. Do not embed a\nspecific activation's policy, sha, principal, or grant in reusable instructions.\n\nDiscover exact schemas with `tools.describe` before first use, then reuse the\nacquired schema; do not reload it for ceremony. Supported, commonly used\noperations:\n\n- `source.read` — `arguments {source: SourceRef, encoding: \"utf8\"}`; returns the\n  content plus a retained acquisition artifact.\n- `workspace.observe` — `arguments {scope: [{root, path, kind}], previous?}`;\n  returns an observation artifact at `result.artifact` (pass that ref, not the\n  top-level operation evidence, where an observation basis is required).\n- `work.write` — `arguments {grant_id, target: SourceRef (sha256 null only for a\n  confirmed-absent file), mode: \"replace\"|\"append\", record: {text, provenance:\n  SourceRef}, interpretation: null|{text, author}, observations: [observation\n  ArtifactRef]}`. Each effect needs a unique request `id`; ensure the target's\n  parent exists and observe the target before writing. Retain the returned\n  postimage and effect evidence.\n\nEach operation used for a 3.0.1 claim needs an established compatible contract.\nReading opaque bytes under an honest legacy acquisition contract makes only that\nacquisition claim; it does not upgrade a lifecycle profile.\n\n## Acquire only the deciding context (SK-05)\n\nAcquire the deciding Product, requirements, scenarios, frame, and owner material\nthrough the declared source routes, plus the specific sources your change\ntouches. Retain each acquisition's evidence id. Keep in the working context the\nexact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority, required evidence,\ncapability limits, return consumer, and invalidators. Equal candidate bytes do\nnot erase a differing retained assessment, an unresolved obligation, or a\ncurrentness fact — those still require different handling. A sufficient task\ncontext implies no general optimal-compression claim.\n\n## When a tool fails (SK-04 discriminator, Q06)\n\n- If an operation returns an **unsupported method** (for example native\n  `results.conjoin`, which `tools.describe` lists as unsupported), retain the\n  actual refusal and withhold the dependent claim. Do not relabel another path\n  as the result.\n- If an operation returns an **execution error**, retain the error and the\n  unknown-effect state, withhold the dependent claim, and identify the next\n  supported re-entry.\n- Never replace a required tool result with an invented check, a narrative of\n  intended calls, or an unqualified alternate path. Independent useful work may\n  continue within the grant, but the blocked claim stays blocked.\n\n## After an uncertain effect (Q08)\n\nIf an effect's completion is uncertain (timeout, interrupted acknowledgment),\nreconcile by re-observing the target before any retry. A repeated request must\nnot duplicate an uncertain effect, and a timeout does not prove rollback. See\n`stdo-continuation`.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` section 2 and\n`REFERENCE_FRAME.md` sections 3 and 11 for context sufficiency, currentness, and\nacquisition; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 and `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` sections 5 and\n7 for result, effects, and disposition; `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for\nactual-path proof semantics.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nTool harmonisation is owned by a_c; this skill consumes supported contracts and\nreports defects, it does not fork tool semantics. Output availability from an\noperation is not semantic acceptance of the result.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011XsCWNPNddpE1KruHHKaz3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
