{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgND8EwQsearBgKGfL64t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bounded correction is done and verified. Nothing further is needed, so here is the closing record.\n\n**Outcome.** `outputs/greeting.txt` now contains exactly `Hello, Ada.` followed by one newline, as R1 and D1 require for the current name in inputs/name.txt. Nothing else in the workspace changed. No ticket, review stage, Git action, or new file was created, matching GOALS.md and the proportionality rule.\n\n**Basis verified before writing.** The stdo manager reports the pinned cut v3.0.1-rc.1 installed and valid, with the manifest hash equal to the one fixture_product.json pins, and no member failures. The worker policy hash matched the value in TOOLING.md.\n\n**How the change was made.** All work went through the configured a_c tools under the grant named in TOOLING.md. The requirement, design, and input name were acquired by governed source.read. The output parent directory and the target file were observed separately immediately before the write. One work.write in replace mode produced the new content, with the design cited as provenance and an interpretation recording the input hash, the preimage hash, and the derivation.\n\n| Artifact | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| outputs/greeting.txt | `Hello, Grace.\\n`, 14 bytes, sha256 dbfa3fca… | `Hello, Ada.\\n`, 12 bytes, sha256 8b1560f3… |\n| unrelated/sentinel.txt | sha256 56686d9c… | unchanged |\n| Governing files (requirement, design, TASK.md, product, OWNER.json, input) | | all unchanged |\n\n**Verification.** A governed re-observation diffed against the pre-write observation shows exactly the one expected change. A separate governed observation of the sentinel shows it intact. A native byte dump and hash comparison agree, and the hash of the literal expected string equals the file's hash.\n\n**One retained refusal, not an effect problem.** My first post-write observation was refused with cause \"basis_ambiguous\" because I widened the scope to include the sentinel while passing a previous observation. The tool requires identical scopes for a diff. I redid it with the original scope and it succeeded. The refusal is retained in a_c evidence as my request error.\n\n**Evidence ids for the record.** Write effect evidence sha256:879995b7…, writer result artifact sha256:d6d3a05c…, post-write diff observation artifact sha256:f74fe46a…, sentinel observation artifact sha256:ef651a98…. The tools.describe response states that output availability is not semantic acceptance, so acceptance remains with the owner's source-first assessment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3053,"cache_read_input_tokens":76944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3053},"output_tokens":694,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1050b227-946f-4be0-992d-736b9ee8c71a","uuid":"9b9610f7-e82e-4633-9ff9-e599c5358d93","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:01:38.034Z","request_id":"req_011CgND8EbL1bMADHuZdneAR"}
